Changed the event consumer to re-read its configured LLM Model on a TTL (`ingestion.triage.model_cache_seconds`, default 60 seconds) instead of holding it for the life of the process, so unticking `Enabled` on a provider or model - or correcting its prices - reaches a consumer that is already running.
Changed the LLM triage attach path to read its target ticket inside the transaction and under a row lock, so a concurrent human edit or a second consumer is no longer overwritten by a stale row.
Changed `nautobot-server eventconsumer --dry-run` to start without the optional `llm` extra: a dry run consults no model, so it no longer refuses to start for want of the means to call one, and its banner says `triage skipped (dry run)` rather than naming a model nothing will call.
Changed `usage_retention_days` to be validated when it is read: a value of `0` deleted every LLM usage record rather than keeping them for no days, and is now refused. A failed prune is also retried rather than blocked for 24 hours.
Changed the LLM Provider and LLM Model filtersets to offer the `tags` filter, matching Event Ticket.
